rances on  80 staples like Remington Steele  nowadays she's still mostly known for  Highlander in the mid 90s she had a 46  episode run on medical drama Chicago  Hope but her film roles have fizzled out  a bit nevertheless she's maintained an  active career with dozens of credits to  her name in the last 10 years she  recently had a multi-episode arc on how  to get away with a murder and appeared  on an episode of the Netflix sitcom  flaked the unofficial spokesman for  Scotland in general masculinity Sean  Connery was by far the biggest celebrity  in the Highlander cast at the time of  the film's released he was already  famous for his turns and Zardoz the man  who would be king and of course Darby  O'Gill and the little people oh and he  also apparently played a spy with the  codename double-oh-seven and several  action flicks Connery's portrayal of a  katana wielding Egyptian immortal was  like much of Highlander puzzling he  appeared in a few more blockbusters in  the following decades but then in 2003  he retired from acting he's since  returned only for voice work first in  the 2005 video game adaptation of From  Russia With Love  amongst Lucasfilm to be playing James  Bond again then he voiced the title  character in the universally maligned  cartoon serve Billy in 2012 which he  seemed to do at least in part because he  was allowed to record his lines in the  Bahamas in recent years he's been a bit  of a reckless which some have speculated  has something to do with his status as a  tax exile when it comes to Clancy Brown  the question isn't so much where is he  now as much as its where isn't he the  towering character actor who went full  maniac as Highlanders Kurgan has stayed  busier than just about anyone in the  cast when Highlander came out he was  still mostly unknown having only  appeared in a handful of movies  including the cult classic The  Adventures of Buckaroo Banzai across the  8th dimension he'd also rounded out his  classical dramatic training with an  episode of The Dukes of Hazzard but  Highlander was his first major gig  according to Russell Mulcahy on was so  nervous during his fight scene with Sean  Connery that he accidentally smashed the  flat side of his sword into a table this  shattered the weapon and sent a short of  it flying past Connery's head thus  convincing Connery to use his stunt  double a little more often since then  Browne has been working pretty much  non-stop his face should be recognizable  to fans of The Shawshank Redemption and  Starship Troopers among other things but  perhaps the most beloved role of his  entire career is a voice only one as  he's played mr. Krabs in hundreds of  episodes of Spongebob Squarepants and in  2019 he made a big splash in the Star  Wars universe as berg in an episode of  the mandalorian the death of Heather  Connor MacLeod first wife served two  important purposes in Highlander first  if foreshadowed the lonely life that  Connor had in store for him as an  immortal doomed to watch those he cared  about succumbed to sickness and death  second it gave Queens Brian May an  excuse to write the song who wants to  live forever which he has said was  inspired by an early cut of the film  Heather was played by English actress BD  Edney another newcomer at the time of  filming she never broke out  internationally the way some of her cast  mates did nevertheless she's maintained  a steady stage and TV career in the  United Kingdom her most notable recent  credit is the historical drama series  Poldark which tells the story of a  British soldier returning home after the  American Revolution check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about your favorite stuff  or coming soon subscribe to our YouTube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

